WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
- Let's close things out

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.210
with something that
might make us all smile.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.541
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.541 --> 00:00:06.960
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.460
You all know Danielle Kartes.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.560
We've had her on many, many times.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.080
She's taught us how to
make overflowing lava cake,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.050
the Olive Garden's pasta fagioli.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:19.020
She's even shown us secrets
to dining al fresco.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.820
Danielle seriously
works some magic, y'all.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.940
Now she's got her own vodka
line called Fluorescence.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.970
This is a woman who
chases the right dreams.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.500
We have Danielle on the line right now

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.230
watching on KOMO 4 at 2:00 PM in Seattle.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.101
What's up, Danielle!

00:00:33.101 --> 00:00:34.272
(crowd cheering)

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:35.105
- Hi.

00:00:35.105 --> 00:00:36.510
Oh my gosh. I'm so excited to see you.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.070
This is so good.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.060
- [Kelly] I'm very excited.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.100
I think I have a drink right
here, so it's great to see you.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:41.933
That's so cool.

00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:43.980
So what made you want
to launch a vodka brand?

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.003
And thank you.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.550
- Oh my gosh. I know this is so cool.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.310
So it's called Fluorescence,
which means to be in bloom.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.143
- [Kelly] Oh?

00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:52.080
- And I think that we are 40,

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.940
you and I both turned 40 this year.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.740
It was really important
for me to create something,

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.050
first of all, that didn't
taste like gasoline.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.540
I feel like we needed
something that was delicious

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.380
and flavorful.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.150
It's grapefruit and pomelo.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.460
Is that not the most
delicious cocktail ever?

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.750
- Like, you missed my
actual initial reaction

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.220
- [Danielle] It's the smoothest.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.690
- It's so good.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.890
- Yep.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.020
It's so good.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.180
And it took two years to formulate this.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.820
I partnered with one of our
clients, Heritage Distilling.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.910
We came up with a beautiful
vodka that's all natural.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.050
It tastes wonderful.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.180
And it speaks to women like you and me.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.760
I feel like everything is
marketed to 20-somethings,

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.860
and I'm like, we're in
the prime of our lives.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.030
We are flourishing.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.440
We're doing drop off.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.270
We're running empires.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.430
And I want women to chase their dreams.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.500
You don't have to have all
the means in the world.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.080
You just got to get out there
and get a vodka line going.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.237
Okay?

00:01:41.237 --> 00:01:42.237
(laughing)

00:01:42.237 --> 00:01:43.590
(crowd clapping)

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.330
- That is some great advice.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.070
Thank you Danielle, as always.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:48.030
We love you so much here.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.740
This is dang good.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.860
I'm liking your post right now
and I'm enjoying your drink

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.404
constantly.

00:01:54.404 --> 00:01:55.237
- Thank you.

00:01:55.237 --> 00:01:56.724
To being in bloom.

00:01:56.724 --> 00:01:57.557
- Absolutely. Okay.

00:01:57.557 --> 00:02:00.660
So usually this is the point
when we give our guest money,

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.760
courtesy of Pilot Pen Makers of G2,

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.860
the go-to pen of The Kelly Clarkson show.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:05.700
Ding.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.660
But come on.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.910
Danielle's got all her cookware,
she's got a vodka line.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.050
She don't need money.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.690
So today we're giving
someone in the audience

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.280
a thousand dollars from Pilot Pen.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.430
So the check is under someone's chair.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:18.543
So who got it?

00:02:19.496 --> 00:02:20.434
Who got it?

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.767
(drum roll)

00:02:24.724 --> 00:02:28.557
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:02:31.114 --> 00:02:31.947
- Yeah!

00:02:33.785 --> 00:02:35.535
Stand up!

00:02:35.535 --> 00:02:36.368
It's me. It's me

00:02:36.368 --> 00:02:37.817
- Stand up. Stand up.

00:02:37.817 --> 00:02:40.200
What's your name? Where are you from?

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.370
- My name is Kimberly Kay

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.816
and I'm from St. George, Utah.

00:02:43.816 --> 00:02:44.649
(crowd clapping)

00:02:44.649 --> 00:02:46.320
- Okay. Well this is for you.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.395
What you gonna do with that money?

00:02:48.395 --> 00:02:49.945
- I don't know something.

00:02:49.945 --> 00:02:50.988
(crowd laughing)

00:02:50.988 --> 00:02:52.113
- Oh my God, I love you so much!

00:02:52.113 --> 00:02:53.700
Well have some fun with it.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.993
Congratulations.

